#% BinInit source package definition.
#% Compile with: gshai -et bininit.shaye main.shay

#% ===== BININIT ENTRY SOURCE =====
#% This file is the readable source used to generate bininit.shaye.
#% Compile it with: gshai -et bininit.shaye main.shay
#% The generated .shaye is a binary entry package, not a source file.
#% BinInit works with logical BaseFul sectors managed by BaseFul.
#% It does not expose raw physical disk sectors or direct disk access.
#% This entry defines four BinInit syntax families.
#% Hexadecimal numeric literals use the 0x prefix.
#% Binary numeric literals use the 0b prefix.
#% The selectsector form chooses a logical BaseFul sector.
#% The expdatabinary form expands selected sector data as binary.
#% instxtexit/> is core Shay syntax and is not declared here.
#% No extra sector commands are invented by this entry.
#% The definitions below are syntax metadata for the entry loader.
#% Runtime execution requires matching lexer, parser, and runtime support.
#% A syntax declaration alone does not implement disk or sector operations.

#% ===== HEXADECIMAL LITERAL =====
#% The hexadecimal family is named hexnum.
#% The prefix is exactly 0x after the opening delimiter.
#% Digits 0 through 9 are valid hexadecimal digits.
#% Letters A through F are valid hexadecimal digits.
#% Letters a through f are valid hexadecimal digits.
#% The closing delimiter terminates the numeric literal.
#% The value is interpreted as a number, not as a string.
#% Leading zeroes do not change the represented value.
#% A hexadecimal literal must contain at least one digit.
#% A hexadecimal literal cannot contain a sign inside its digits.
#% A sign, if supported by an expression, belongs outside the literal.
#% Whitespace is not permitted inside the delimited literal.
#% Invalid hexadecimal characters must be diagnosed.
#% An unterminated hexadecimal literal must be diagnosed.
#% The implementation must detect numeric overflow.

#% ===== BINARY LITERAL =====
#% The binary family is named binnum.
#% The prefix is exactly 0b after the opening delimiter.
#% Only zero and one are valid binary digits.
#% The closing delimiter terminates the numeric literal.
#% The value is interpreted as a number, not as a string.
#% Leading zeroes do not change the represented value.
#% A binary literal must contain at least one digit.
#% A binary literal cannot contain other decimal digits.
#% A binary literal cannot contain hexadecimal letters.
#% Whitespace is not permitted inside the delimited literal.
#% Invalid binary characters must be diagnosed.
#% An unterminated binary literal must be diagnosed.
#% The implementation must detect numeric overflow.
#% Binary and hexadecimal values should share numeric expression rules.
#% The literal form must remain unambiguous with ordinary Shay symbols.

#% ===== LOGICAL SECTOR SELECTION =====
#% The selection family is named selectsector.
#% The command accepts one value identifying a logical BaseFul sector.
#% The value is evaluated using the active Shay expression rules.
#% The selected sector belongs to BaseFul's logical sector model.
#% Selection does not select a physical disk sector.
#% Selection does not grant raw device access.
#% BaseFul validates whether the requested logical sector exists.
#% A missing logical sector must produce a clear runtime error.
#% An invalid sector identifier must not change the current selection.
#% A successful selection becomes the current logical sector.
#% The selected sector is scoped to the active BaseFul context.
#% The operation must not silently create a new sector.
#% The operation must not modify sector contents.
#% The command has no implicit output unless the runtime specifies it.
#% The selected sector is the input to the expansion operation.

#% ===== BINARY DATA EXPANSION =====
#% The expansion family is named expdatabinary.
#% The command uses the currently selected logical BaseFul sector.
#% The command expands that sector's data into a binary representation.
#% The operation reads through BaseFul's logical data interface.
#% The operation does not read a physical disk sector directly.
#% The operation does not change the selected sector.
#% The operation does not modify the sector's stored data.
#% The output representation must be deterministic.
#% Each byte is represented using eight binary digits.
#% Byte order follows the logical data order supplied by BaseFul.
#% An empty logical sector produces an empty binary representation.
#% A missing selection must produce a clear runtime error.
#% A failed BaseFul read must be reported to the caller.
#% The operation must not silently truncate sector data.
#% The operation must not silently pad missing data.

#% ===== COMPILER AND INTERPRETER EXPECTATIONS =====
#% gshai and shaii must agree on the declared syntax.
#% The compiler must reject malformed literal tokens.
#% The interpreter must reject malformed literal tokens.
#% Both tools must report the source location of syntax errors.
#% The compiler must preserve ordinary Shay expression precedence.
#% The interpreter must preserve ordinary Shay expression precedence.
#% The entry is optional when a program does not use BinInit syntax.
#% A program activates this entry with $useentry bininit.
#% The entry filename stem is the name used by $useentry.
#% The package is discovered through the configured entry directories.
#% The binary package must be validated before its records are registered.
#% Malformed packages must not partially register syntax definitions.
#% Existing alias-only .shaye packages remain supported.
#% Unknown package opcodes must be rejected safely.
#% The package format is not encryption or a security boundary.

#% ===== SAFETY BOUNDARIES =====
#% BaseFul owns the logical sector abstraction.
#% BinInit requests operations through BaseFul only.
#% BinInit does not bypass BaseFul validation.
#% BinInit does not expose arbitrary device paths.
#% BinInit does not issue raw read or write system calls.
#% BinInit does not write sector data during selection.
#% BinInit does not write sector data during binary expansion.
#% The expansion command is read-only.
#% A future write operation would require a separate explicit design.
#% No future write operation is implied by these declarations.
#% No physical geometry is exposed by these declarations.
#% No partition table is modified by these declarations.
#% No boot record is modified by these declarations.
#% No filesystem metadata is modified by these declarations.
#% Errors must leave BaseFul's logical sector state consistent.

#% ===== EXTENSION SCOPE =====
#% This entry is named bininit.
#% Its syntax definitions are hexnum, binnum, selectsector, and expdatabinary.
#% The entry does not redefine instxt or instxtexit.
#% The entry does not redefine existing control-flow keywords.
#% The entry does not add unrequested list or backup commands.
#% The entry does not add unrequested restore commands.
#% The entry does not add unrequested sector deletion commands.
#% The entry does not add unrequested sector enumeration commands.
#% The entry does not add unrequested physical disk commands.
#% The entry does not add unrequested import or export commands.
#% The entry does not add unrequested comparison commands.
#% The entry does not add unrequested formatting commands.
#% The entry does not add unrequested raw memory access.
#% The entry remains optional for normal Shay programs.
#% The syntax names remain lowercase as required by $useentry.

$entrysyndef hexnum
    ::0x[0-9A-Fa-f]+::
finish

$entrysyndef binnum
    ::0b[01]+::
finish

$entrysyndef selectsector
    :$selectsector value
finish

$entrysyndef expdatabinary
    :$expdatabinary
finish
